# Request
#
# Two mutually-exclusive target modes, selected by `use_joint_target`:
#   - use_joint_target == false (default): move to `target_pose` (Cartesian,
#     ra_flange frame), as before.
#   - use_joint_target == true: move to the explicit joint target given by
#     the six ra_* fields below, ignoring `target_pose` and `estimate`
#     entirely (no Cartesian collision-object scoping applies to a joint
#     goal). Named fields are used instead of a float64[6] array so a
#     mis-ordered joint list can't silently swap two joints - each value is
#     bound to its joint by name, not by position.

geometry_msgs/Pose target_pose
pcl_package/PrimitiveEstimate estimate

bool use_joint_target
float64 ra_shoulder_pan_joint
float64 ra_shoulder_lift_joint
float64 ra_elbow_joint
float64 ra_wrist_1_joint
float64 ra_wrist_2_joint
float64 ra_wrist_3_joint

bool wait_for_confirmation
float64 velocity_scaling
---
# Response
bool success
string outcome
string reason
